{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "פקד פקדתי אתכם", :translit "pakod pakad'ti etchem", :gloss "visiting I have visited you"} {:he "פקוד", :translit "pakud", :gloss "withheld / accounted"} {:he "ולא נפקד ממנו איש", :translit "v'lo nifkad mimenu ish", :gloss "and not a man was missing from us"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "פקד פקדתי אתכם", :b "פקוד"}], :frame {:text "The word פקידה connotes both divine visitation and withholding or assignment. The phrase ולא נפקד ממנו איש appears in Numbers 31:49 after the war with Midian, where the officers report that not a single Israelite soldier was lost.", :sources ["Numbers 31:49"]}} {:quotes [{:he "העשוי", :translit "ha'asuy", :gloss "the made / the prepared"} {:he "ואת העשוי לכם במצרים", :translit "v'et ha'asuy lachem b'mitzrayim", :gloss "and the made for you in Egypt"} {:he "כל הזהב העשוי למלאכה", :translit "kol ha'zahav ha'asuy la'melachah", :gloss "all the gold made for the work"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["ואת העשוי לכם במצרים" "כל הזהב העשוי למלאכה"]}], :frame {:text "The Israelites received gold and valuables from the Egyptians at the Exodus as described in Exodus 12:36. The gold used for the Tabernacle is enumerated in Exodus 38:24. The link between Egyptian wealth and Tabernacle materials reflects the identification of Israel's spoils with the subsequent building contributions.", :sources ["Exodus 12:36" "Exodus 38:24"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :gematria, :a "פקד פקדתי אתכם", :a-value 1239, :b "פקוד", :b-value 190, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? false} {:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["ואת העשוי לכם במצרים" "כל הזהב העשוי למלאכה"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "ואת העשוי לכם במצרים", :refs ["Exodus 3:16"], :n 1, :lens :exact} {:phrase "כל הזהב העשוי למלאכה", :refs ["Exodus 38:24"], :n 1, :lens :exact}]}], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:13:23.593277654Z", :mod